    "topic": "Kinematics - Uniform Acceleration",
    "questionNumber": 1,
    "statement": "A particle moves in a straight line with a constant acceleration. It changes its velocity from 10 ms-1 to 20 ms-1 while passing through a distance 135 m in t second. The value of t is:",
    "statementImages": [],
    "options": [
      {
        "optionIndex": 1,
        "label": "A",
        "text": "12",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "markedPercentage": "14.2%"
      },
      {
        "optionIndex": 2,
        "label": "B",
        "text": "9",
        "isCorrect": true,
        "markedPercentage": "20.12%"
      },
      {
        "optionIndex": 3,
        "label": "C",
        "text": "10",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "markedPercentage": "35.4%"
      },
      {
        "optionIndex": 4,
        "label": "D",
        "text": "1.8",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "markedPercentage": "30.28%"
      }
    ],
    "correctOption": 2,
    "correctAnswer": "9",
    "accuracy": "20.12% of students got it right",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "solutionText": "Using kinematic equation:\nv^2 = u^2 + 2as\n(20)^2 = (10)^2 + 2(a)(135)\n400 - 100 = 270a => 300 = 270a => a = 10/9 m/s^2\n\nNow using:\nv = u + at\n20 = 10 + (10/9)t\n10 = (10/9)t => t = 9 s."
  },
