  {
    "id": "pw-phy-c11-misl-005",
    "subject": "Physics",
    "chapter": "Motion in a Straight Line",
    "topic": "Kinematics - Free Fall and Released Packets",
    "questionNumber": 5,
    "statement": "A helicopter rises from rest on the ground vertically upwards with a constant acceleration g. A food packet is dropped from the helicopter when it is at a height h. The time taken by the packet to reach the ground is close to [ g is the acceleration due to gravity]",
    "statementImages": [],
    "options": [
      {
        "optionIndex": 1,
        "label": "A",
        "text": "t = 3.4 \\sqrt{\\frac{h}{g}}",
        "isCorrect": true,
        "markedPercentage": "35.18%"
      },
      {
        "optionIndex": 2,
        "label": "B",
        "text": "t = 1.8 \\sqrt{\\frac{h}{g}}",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "markedPercentage": "26.35%"
      },
      {
        "optionIndex": 3,
        "label": "C",
        "text": "t = \\sqrt{\\frac{2h}{3g}}",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "markedPercentage": "30.39%"
      },
      {
        "optionIndex": 4,
        "label": "D",
        "text": "\\frac{2}{3} \\sqrt{\\frac{h}{g}}",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "markedPercentage": "8.23%"
      }
    ],
    "correctOption": 1,
    "correctAnswer": "t = 3.4 \\sqrt{h/g}",
    "accuracy": "35.18% of students got it right",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "solutionText": "When the helicopter reaches height h with acceleration g from rest:\nv^2 = 0 + 2gh => v = \\sqrt{2gh} (directed upward).\nFor the dropped packet:\nTaking ground as origin:\n0 = h + vt - 0.5 g t^2\n0 = h + \\sqrt{2gh} t - 0.5 g t^2\n0.5 g t^2 - \\sqrt{2gh} t - h = 0\nt = [\\sqrt{2gh} + \\sqrt{2gh + 4(0.5g)(h)}] / g = [\\sqrt{2gh} + \\sqrt{4gh}] / g = (\\sqrt{2} + 2) \\sqrt{h/g} \u2248 (1.414 + 2) \\sqrt{h/g} = 3.414 \\sqrt{h/g} \u2248 3.4 \\sqrt{h/g}."
  },
  {
