    "correctOption": 2,
    "correctAnswer": "(a \u2212 g)",
    "accuracy": "46.66% of students got it right",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "solutionText": "To find the effective acceleration of the body, we analyze the directions of the accelerations acting on it:\nUpward Acceleration (a): The body is actively thrown or propelled upwards with an acceleration of a.\nDownward Acceleration (g): The acceleration due to gravity always acts vertically downwards towards the Earth.\nSince these two accelerations act in exactly opposite directions along the vertical line of motion, the net or effective upward acceleration is: Effective Acceleration = a \u2212 g."
